Well , even the easy installations will sometimes give you problems. I
am talking from the point of view of a computer novice. I installed
SUSE 9.1 on my home computer, and it took me about 1 week to get it
running right. The installation was easy but i messed something up
while upgrading it to the newest stuff. You can buy this at the store
or download it for free. Be prepared to do research on all stages of
learning your new system. 

This is the page i used for research. http://www.linux.org/
This page also list other beginner friendly distributions and has a
lesson to get you started with simple commands. I also went and
bought linux in a nutshell (O'Reilly)for a handy list of the Linux
commands. There are pages on the net that will give you the same
info. 




